CSKG spike layer (loaded locally from data/raw/cskg/, src/cskg/)
----------------------------------------------------------------
The FULL CSKG extract is NOT shipped in this repository: the files
under data/raw/cskg/ are gitignored local downloads. (A trimmed
subset for the fork feeder DOES ship — see the next section.) The
src/cskg/ package is a self-contained spike (2026-11-09) that loads

  CSKG: The CommonSense Knowledge Graph
  Ilievski, Szekely & Zhang, ESWC 2021
  USC Information Sciences Institute
  https://github.com/usc-isi-i2/cskg — data: Zenodo record 4331372

CSKG unifies ConceptNet, WordNet, FrameNet, ATOMIC, Roget's Thesaurus,
a Wikidata subset and Visual Genome. Its distributors offer it under
the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License
(CC BY-SA 4.0) per the project documentation; the Zenodo record lists
CC BY 4.0. AnSci treats it as CC BY-SA 4.0. The component sources keep
their own terms (see the CSKG documentation); the loader preserves each
edge's source dataset so provenance survives into the chat's answers.

CSKG fork feeder bundle (data/cskg/, src/ansci/cskg-ingest.ts)
--------------------------------------------------------------
The bundle in data/cskg/ IS shipped in this repository: a trimmed
subset of the CSKG graph described in the section above, produced
2026-11-17 by running the fork feeder's own mapping rules
(src/ansci/cskg-feed.ts — 21 relations: twelve concept relations
under the both-ends-classified rule, nine ATOMIC relations under
event-rule anchoring) over the locally installed full extract and
keeping what the feeder keeps: 80,466 edges of the extract's
6,001,531. The generation record — source, stage counts, per-source
and per-relation counts — stands in data/cskg/manifest.json; the
staged measurement procedure is recorded as Run 2 of the CSKG trim
measurement (2026-11-17).

The bundle is distributed under the same terms AnSci treats CSKG
under: the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
License (CC BY-SA 4.0). Attribution: Ilievski, Szekely & Zhang,
"CSKG: The CommonSense Knowledge Graph", ESWC 2021, USC Information
Sciences Institute; data: Zenodo record 4331372. ShareAlike applies
to the bundle data: redistributions of the bundle, modified or not,
carry CC BY-SA 4.0. Each edge keeps its source code (AT, CN, CN|WN,
WN) so the component sources' provenance survives; the component
sources keep their own terms (see the CSKG documentation). The full
extract remains a local install (scripts/install.mjs downloads it
from Zenodo) and is the source a future re-trim would run against.

